    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0525" n="451" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg451"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 138.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 5, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 4th of
                    March, No. 99, containing a statement of your proceedings with regard to Señor
                    Sinibaldo de Mas, the Spanish minister, who visited China during the past year
                    for the purpose of concluding a treaty with that government. Your action in the
                    premises is fully approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretar.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c.,&amp;c.,&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
